{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The preamble makes Wells Fargo Bank, N.A. the Auction Agent acting \"not in its individual capacity but solely as agent of WELLS FARGO BANK, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION (the 'Tmstee')\" — the same entity is named as both principal and agent, so the capacity in which it acts and is liable is indeterminate. The garbled defined term \"Tmstee\" compounds the problem because the operative sections (e.g., 3.1(a)) all refer to \"the Trustee.\"", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The recital defines the four series collectively as the \"Series 2004 Bonds\" and then says the same set is \"sometimes referred to together herein as the 'Series 2004 Auction Bonds',\" equating two terms that Section 1.3(f) treats as distinct references. Which instrument-wide term governs an obligation is therefore open to construction.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"BD is to perform certain duties set forth herein\" identifies no duties and gives no boundary to \"certain duties,\" leaving open whether BD's obligations are exhausted by the express sections or extend further. The recital can be argued either to limit BD to enumerated tasks or to acknowledge a broader undertaking.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The recital makes the Auction Rate subject to two unstated escape hatches (\"except as provided therein\" and \"except as otherwise provided therein\") located in the Indenture, while Section 2.1(a)-(b) incorporates only the Auction Procedures and Settlement Procedures into this Agreement. What rate applies when the Auction Procedures do not produce one therefore cannot be resolved from the four corners of this instrument.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
